# Per-run outputs of the proposal tooling. Every one of these is rewritten by the next
# `final.mjs` / `supplied.mjs` run, and the copy that matters is the one placed beside the PDF in
# docs/proposals/. Committing them would mean a dirty tree after every render and a second, stale
# copy of each proposal's cells — the drift this repo already has a rule about.
#
# `results/` is NOT here and must not be: the annealer's candidates are committed on purpose —
# `final.mjs` is driven from them, so they are the searched proposals' record, not scratch.
*.html
proposal.json
proposal-import.txt
supplied.json
supplied-import.txt

# Search scratch: the per-seed STARTING copies and the optimiser's raw output. Anything a rendered
# PDF cites in its alternatives table is copied to a stable name and committed instead — a document
# that names a candidate has to be reproducible, and a gitignored candidate makes it not.
# A per-seed INPUT copy is named <design>-s<seed>.json by convention; the optimiser's raw output is
# <input>-optimised.json. Neither is committed.
seed*.json
*-s[0-9]*.json
best-so-far.json
*-optimised.json
# A driver's run SUMMARY is the same class: wl4-run.mjs rewrites this on every run, and the
# figures that matter end up in the proposal's own meta beside its PDF.
wl4-results.json
